{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, exposing all controllable and uncontrollable events. The specification encodes a safe, coverage-oriented supervisor: in clear/search states, random_walk is preferred for exploration; move_forward is used for short progress; upon obstacles, recovery uses short directed turns (CW for left, CCW for right, CW for front by default), and only escalates to full_rotate after repeated front blocks. Recovery states are one-shot and return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. All obstacle events preempt motion, and no state enables both rotate directions or forward/turn simultaneously. The design avoids oscillation and ensures steady progress.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant for motion/perception interface and specification for safe exploration policy",
    "Bias toward random_walk in clear/search, use move_forward for short progress, and use minimal, directed turn recovery for obstacles"
  ],
